/-!
# Principal-quotient conditions for a fractional monogenic algebra

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 0334, Step 5, properties (2), (3)(a), (3)(b).
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-monogenic-principal-quotient-conditions).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

/-- The nonzero generator in a maximal ideal satisfies the three quotient conditions
of the analytic-unramifiedness criterion.
Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 0334, Step 5, lines 46179--46221.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-monogenic-principal-quotient-conditions).

Proof:
1. Let `I` be the kernel of `R[T] → R[x]`. For a polynomial vanishing at `x`,
   its leading coefficient times `x` is integral (Tag 00PQ), hence belongs to `R`.
   Subtract the resulting linear relation times the appropriate power of `T` and
   induct on degree. Thus `I` is generated by `cT - d` with `cx = d`.
   Modulo `T` this gives `R[x]/xR[x] = R/J`, where `J = R ∩ xR`.
2. Tag 031T gives no embedded associated primes of `R/J`, all of height one. Transport
   these primes across the quotient identification and localize at the maximal ideal.
   The surviving associated primes are minimal over the localized principal ideal;
   this proves the first assertion.
3. For each surviving prime `q` and its contraction `p`, the ring `R_p` is a DVR
   (Tag 00PD). The valuation of `x` cannot be negative: otherwise `x⁻¹` and `x` would
   both lie in `qR[x]_q`, implying `1` lies there. Thus `x ∈ R_p`, so `R[x]_q = R_p`.
   Iterated localization identifies this with the corresponding associated-prime
   localization of `R[x]_m`. It is regular, proving the second assertion.
4. Since `x ∈ q`, the prime quotient `R[x]/q` is `R/p`. Its localization at `m` is
   Nagata by Tags 032T and 032U and analytically unramified by Tag 0331. This is the
   quotient of `R[x]_m` by the corresponding associated prime, proving the third assertion. -/
theorem adjoin_singleton_atPrime_principal_quotient_conditions
    (R : Type u) (K : Type v) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
    (hR : IsNagataRing R) (x : K) (hx0 : x ≠ 0)
    [IsNoetherianRing (Algebra.adjoin R ({x} : Set K))]
    (m : Ideal (Algebra.adjoin R ({x} : Set K))) [m.IsMaximal]
    (hx : (⟨x, Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_singleton x)⟩ :
      Algebra.adjoin R ({x} : Set K)) ∈ m) :
    let A := Localization.AtPrime m
    let t : A := algebraMap (Algebra.adjoin R ({x} : Set K)) A
      ⟨x, Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_singleton x)⟩
    (∀ p ∈ associatedPrimes A (A ⧸ Ideal.span {t}), (Ideal.span {t}).IsMinimalPrime p) ∧
    (∀ p : associatedPrimes A (A ⧸ Ideal.span {t}),
      IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime p.1)) ∧
    (∀ p ∈ associatedPrimes A (A ⧸ Ideal.span {t}), p.IsAnalyticallyUnramified) := by sorry
